# Pollock's self-defeating argument (Pollock 1995, Cognitive Carpentry):
# Smith is presumed reliable; Smith says that Smith is unreliable; what a
# reliable witness says is true. The argument for "Smith is unreliable"
# rests on Smith's reliability and so defeats itself. Pollock (OSCAR): a
# self-defeating argument is defeated; it defeats nothing, so "Smith is
# reliable" stays justified. Grounded semantics of the abstract framework
# leaves both undecided.
lk.
declare Reliable, Says : bool.
declare says : (Says).
declare testimony : (Reliable -> Says -> ~Reliable).
argument reliable : (Reliable).
by default.
dixi.
counterargument unreliable : (Reliable).
cut (~Reliable) x.
cut (Reliable -> Says -> ~Reliable) th.
axiom testimony.
elim.
next.
elim.
axiom says.
axiom.
elim.
axiom.
dixi.
